itle_tablet":"","after_title":"","card_carousel_id":0,"custom_historical_url":"","polymarket_slug":"south-carolina-senate-election-winner","hide_spread_chart":0,"has_social_media_image":1,"snapshot":{"title":"South Carolina Snapshot","content":"<p><strong>RCP Ranking<span>:<\/span><\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/maps\/senate\/2026\/toss-up\">Leans GOP<\/a><strong><br \/>RCP Avg:<\/strong>\u00a0(((rcp_spread)))<strong><br \/><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>----------PAST KEY RACES----------<\/p>\n<p><strong><strong>2024:\u00a0<\/strong><\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/president\/general\/2024\/south-carolina\/trump-vs-harris\">President<\/a><strong><strong><br \/>2022:<\/strong><\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2022\/senate\/sc\/south_carolina_senate_scott_vs_matthews-7530.html\">Senate<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2022\/governor\/sc\/south_carolina_governor_mcmaster_vs_cunningham-7505.html\">Governor<\/a><strong><br \/>2020:<\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2020\/president\/sc\/south_carolina_trump_vs_biden-6825.html\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2020\/senate\/sc\/south_carolina_senate_graham_vs_harrison-7083.html\">Senate<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2020\/house\/sc\/south_carolina_1st_district_mace_vs_cunningham-7134.html\">SC-1<\/a><strong><br \/>2018:<\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2018\/governor\/sc\/south_carolina_governor_mcmaster_vs_smith-6431.html\">Governor<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2018\/house\/sc\/south_carolina_1st_district_arrington_vs_cunningham-6705.html\">SC-1<\/a><strong><br \/>2016:\u00a0<\/strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/president\/sc\/south_carolina_trump_vs_clinton_vs_johnson_vs_stein-6093.html\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/senate\/sc\/south_carolina_senate_scott_vs_dixon-5985.html\">Senate<\/a>\u00a0<strong><br \/>2014<\/strong>:<span>\u00a0<\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/senate\/sc\/south_carolina_senate_graham_vs_hutto-5101.html\">Senate<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|<span>\u00a0<\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/senate\/sc\/south_carolina_senate_special_election_scott_vs_dickerson-5102.html\">Senate (Special)<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/governor\/sc\/south_carolina_governor_haley_vs_sheheen-3477.html\">Governor<\/a><strong><br \/><\/strong><\/p>"},"dataAnalysis":{"title":"Race Analysis","content":"<p>South Carolina long occupied the type of place in the Electoral College that Washington, D.C., holds today. From 1900 to 1948, no Republican presidential candidate cleared 10 percent of the vote. That changed in 1952 when, suddenly, Dwight Eisenhower nearly carried the state. It took a long time, however, for Democrats to completely collapse. Fritz Hollings held a Senate seat as a Democrat until he retired in 2004 and Democrats won the governorship as recently as 1998.<\/p>\n<p>Since then, the bottom dropped out for state Democrats. No Democrat has won a statewide race in South Carolina since 2006, and Donald Trump carried the state by 18 points in 2024. There were whispers in 2020 that Jaime Harrison might win the Senate election in the state, and he raised $130 million against Lindsey Graham on that basis, the most money any Senate candidate had ever raised.\u00a0He lost by 10 points.<\/p>\n<p>Which brings us to the strangest Senate race of 2026. Graham won a fifth nomination in June with 57 percent against a businessman nobody had heard of, which was itself a sign of how little affection the state\u2019s Republicans had for him. Then, Graham suddenly died in July. Gov. Henry McMaster appointed Graham\u2019s sister, Darline Graham Nordone, to the seat two days later.<\/p>\n<p>Graham Nordone has never held elected office before, and it shows. Asked about national security in a primary debate, she answered, \u201cI\u2019m just going to be honest here. I'm not that informed on national security.\u201d\u00a0For their part, Democrats have nominated Annie Andrews, a Charleston pediatrician who ran against Rep. Nancy Mace in 2022 (she lost by 14 points).<\/p>\n<p>The polling currently shows Graham with a slight lead, although Andrews\u2019 43 percent is not where she would like to be at this point. Under perfect circumstances, the seat might be gettable, but even an unknown appointee with Trump\u2019s endorsement in a state he won by 18 last time is still a heavy favorite. Andrews will struggle to find the roughly 10 points of crossover voting she needs to succeed.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>"},"showLineChart":0,"showBarChart":1,"showLineChartFirst":0,"sideCharts":{"charts_on_top":0,"left_chart_race_id":"7083","right_chart_race_id":"5101"},"show_final_results":0,"chart_data":{"chart_id":"7672","chart_axis_x":null,"chart_grid_x":null,"chart_axis_y":null,"chart_grid_y":null,"chart_min":null,"chart_max":null,"chart_start":null,"chart_end":null,"poll_id":"9115","chart_highlight":null,"chart_days_extend":"7","chart_height":"360","chart_height_mobile":"360","chart_html5":"0","chart_main_percent":"70","chart_spread_percent":"30","chart_spread_range":"10","chart_name_in_tooltips":"0","chart_spread_force_0_y_axis":"1","chart_y_axis_min":null,"chart_y_axis_max":null,"chart_y_axis_min_m":null,"chart_y_axis_max_m":null}},"poll":[{"id":"9115","type":"rcp_average","pollster":"rcp_average","date":"9\/28 - 10\/18","confidenceInterval":"","sampleSize":"","marginError":"","partisan":"","candidate":[{"name":"Graham Nordone","affiliation":"Republican","value":"48.0","status":"1","id":"36026"},{"name":"Andrews","affiliation":"Democrat","valu